{"parentUuid":"862c5ede-5e0c-4cd0-81e1-906e0742dcf6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0187yvq82C6cNBmxhkQFp44n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AVmNPBwnvi5nRbrTQD36qJ","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"AlphaProof DeepMind Lean theorem proving 2026 status"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8078,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"output_tokens":461,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8078},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":461,"cache_read_input_tokens":13113,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8078,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8078,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosHgFsacu26veJcw5ej","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"702e213f-9852-4a40-af70-a417f3ae3f15","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:49:59.500Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"666eae11-0cac-4968-b55c-7afe4fd59cc6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019eH6dzrPXzJvYW8pQupbPE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"VeriPB pseudo-Boolean proof checker CP 2025 LIPIcs\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - StephanGocht/VeriPB: Verifier for pseudo-Boolean proofs · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\"},{\"title\":\"Practically feasible proof logging for pseudo-Boolean optimization | Lund University Publications\",\"url\":\"https://lup.lub.lu.se/search/publication/b5de3846-96d8-4689-874a-e0e3f939175c\"},{\"title\":\"PBLean: Pseudo-Boolean Proof Certificates for Lean 4\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v1\"},{\"title\":\"A Multi-Stage Proof Logging Framework to Certify the Correctness of CP Solvers\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol307-cp2024/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11/LIPIcs.CP.2024.11.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Without Loss of Generality Reasoning in Solution-Improving Maximum Satisfiability\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2024.4\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Certified Reasoning for Binarized Neural Networks Jiong Yang\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol341-sat2025/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.32/LIPIcs.SAT.2025.32.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"VERIPB and CAKEPB in the SAT Competition 2023\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about VeriPB, the pseudo-Boolean proof checker, and its connection to CP 2025 and LIPIcs:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**VeriPB Overview:**\nVeriPB is a tool for verifying refutations (proofs of unsatisfiability) and more (such as verifying that a valid solution is found) written in python and c++.\n\n**CP 2025 Publication:**\nAn efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization was presented at the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025), published in Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), Volume 340, pp. 21:1-21:27.\n\n**Research Focus:**\nWhile pseudo-Boolean proof logging had mostly consisted of proof-of-concept works far from delivering the performance required for real-world deployment, the work presents an efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization. The work implements proof logging for the full range of techniques in the state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j, including core-guided search and linear programming integration with Farkas certificates and cut generation, and shows that proof logging and checking performance in this much more expressive paradigm is now quite close to the level of SAT solving.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ff108f4f-1962-4739-9d4a-929a42bd2f4f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:01.650Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"666eae11-0cac-4968-b55c-7afe4fd59cc6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3ef613aa-1118-41c8-afd8-66a740640138","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SaAS7CSyMCcnBJ71X2vcwu","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CakePB verified proof checker CakeML CP 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Verified Proof Checking\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/checkers.html\"},{\"title\":\"MIAO / Software / CakePB · GitLab\",\"url\":\"https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/cakepb\"},{\"title\":\"End-to-End Verification for Subgraph Solving\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/aaai24-verified-subgraphs.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The verified CakeML compiler backend | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/330851837_The_verified_CakeML_compiler_backend\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://jakobnordstrom.se/docs/publications/DocumentationVeriPBandCakePBforSATcompetition2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - tanyongkiam/cake_lpr: LPR proof checking with CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/tanyongkiam/cake_lpr\"},{\"title\":\"CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML\",\"url\":\"https://research.chalmers.se/en/publication/531575\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-72013-1_12\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7984575/\"}]\n\nI've found information about CakePB and its relation to CakeML and CP 2025. Here's what I found:\n\n## CakePB - Verified Proof Checker\n\nCakePB is a formally verified proof checker for pseudo-Boolean reasoning for various combinatorial solving and optimization problems based on the CakeML ecosystem.\n\nCakePB and cake_lpr tools are used to audit solver outputs in the annual international SAT solving competitions.\n\n## CP 2025 Connection\n\nThe verified proof checker CakePB only supports a \"kernel\" subset of commands, where the intended workflow for formally verified proof checking is to use VeriPB as a preprocessor to compile augmented proofs into the kernel format to be formally checked by CakePB. In the SAT competition 2025, the only supported option is to run both VeriPB and CakePB.\n\n## Key Features\n\nBy combining and extending the VeriPB and CakePB tools, formally verified end-to-end proof checking is provided that the input and preprocessed output MaxSAT problem instances have the same optimal value.\n\nAs of February 16, 2025, cake_lpr performance was improved by around 5-10% and its compiled binary size was reduced by around 20%.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7a82d497-824a-46a6-98cd-8ba42cd60dc9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:02.225Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3ef613aa-1118-41c8-afd8-66a740640138","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6759822a-c157-4fd4-b572-2ffc44dea1eb","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018F4bdvAq3egC4NqRxrfKsK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT DRAT LRAT proof output sat_parameters\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/master/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding OR-Tools CP-SAT DRAT and LRAT proof output with sat_parameters:\n\n## Proof Output Parameters\n\nOR-Tools CP-SAT includes an `output_lrat_proof` parameter that, when true, outputs an LRAT proof. Additionally, there is a `check_drat_proof` parameter that, when true, outputs a DRAT proof that all the clauses inferred by the solver are valid to a file.\n\n## Constraints and Limitations\n\nBoth DRAT and LRAT proof features have specific constraints: As of November/December 2025, these features only work for pure SAT problems, with num_workers = 1, cp_model_presolve = false, linearization_level <= 1, and symmetry_level <= 1.\n\n## DRAT Proof Verification\n\nOR-Tools includes a drat_writer.h component that writes UNSAT proofs in the DRAT format, which allows checking the correctness of an UNSAT proof with the third party program DRAT-trim.\n\nThese parameters are part of the `sat_parameters.proto` file, which defines the SAT solver parameters and also contains max-SAT and CP parameters.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"aa59659c-ac57-4a9f-ae8a-d3443642c790","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:04.485Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6759822a-c157-4fd4-b572-2ffc44dea1eb","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c0bc89f1-26cc-42ee-aee5-4e08107290ad","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QGzg54o6cHk5YmoRBGwCmS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Alethe proof format cvc5 Lean Coq verification 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Proof format: Alethe — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.0/proofs/output_alethe.html\"},{\"title\":\"Alethe: Towards a Generic SMT Proof Format (extended ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.02354\"},{\"title\":\"Carcara: An Efficient Proof Checker and Elaborator for SMT Proofs in the Alethe Format | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_19\"},{\"title\":\"The Alethe Proof Format An Evolving Specification and Reference Haniel Barbosa1\",\"url\":\"https://verit.loria.fr/documentation/alethe-spec.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver⋆ Haniel Barbosa3\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/publications/2022/BarbosaBBKLMMMN-TACAS22.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Alethe: Towards a Generic SMT Proof Format (extended abstract)\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/352982246_Alethe_Towards_a_Generic_SMT_Proof_Format_extended_abstract\"},{\"title\":\"Proof format: AletheLF — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.1.2/proofs/output_alf.html\"},{\"title\":\"Proof production — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.2/proofs/proofs.html\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Alethe: Towards a Generic SMT Proof Format (extended abstract) | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Alethe:-Towards-a-Generic-SMT-Proof-Format-Schurr-Fleury/763ce08591dc8416f6da5cde06bcb4675cd3ffaa\"},{\"title\":\"Options — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.2/options.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Alethe proof format, cvc5, and verification with Lean and Coq:\n\n## Alethe Proof Format Overview\n\nThe Alethe proof format is a flexible proof format for SMT solvers based on SMT-LIB. It includes both coarse- and fine-grained steps and was first implemented in the veriT solver.\n\n## Integration with cvc5\n\nUsing the flag proof-format-mode=alethe, cvc5 outputs proofs in the Alethe proof format. The currently supported output proof formats include LFSC, Alethe, and the language of the Lean 4 proof assistant.\n\n## Verification with Proof Assistants\n\nAlethe proofs can be checked via reconstruction within Isabelle/HOL as well as within Coq, the latter via the SMTCoq plugin. Additionally, there is also a high performance Rust proof checker for Alethe, available here.\n\n## Proof Checking Tools\n\nCarcara is an independent proof checker and elaborator for Alethe, implemented in Rust. Alethe is an established SMT proof format generated by the solvers veriT and cvc5, with reconstruction support in the proof assistants Isabelle/HOL and Coq.\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about recent developments in 2026, but they provide comprehensive coverage of the Alethe format's current capabilities and integration with verification tools.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6cd9ed0e-fe22-46b1-81f2-6b1f909ecfae","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:05.044Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c0bc89f1-26cc-42ee-aee5-4e08107290ad","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"862c5ede-5e0c-4cd0-81e1-906e0742dcf6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018u4GgwhL3h3C49CoGzU62g","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cake_lpr verified LRAT checker CaDiCaL SAT competition 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Verified LRAT and LPR Proof Checking with cake_lpr Yong Kiam Tan\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/cakelpr.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in ...\",\"url\":\"https://cakeml.org/tacas21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Results of SAT Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/satcomp25slides.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_26\"},{\"title\":\"cake_lpr: Veriﬁed Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML Yong Kiam Tan1(B)\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-030-72013-1_12.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2024\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2024/output.html\"},{\"title\":\"Faster LRAT Checking Than Solving with CaDiCaL Florian Pollitt #\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] cake_lpr: Verified Propagation Redundancy Checking in CakeML | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/cake_lpr:-Verified-Propagation-Redundancy-Checking-Tan-Heule/a23f1afd3c101e136f810e2ceb74dad295aa2b6f\"},{\"title\":\"Faster LRAT Checking than Solving with CaDiCaL 1 Florian Pollitt # 2\",\"url\":\"https://m-fleury.github.io/ox-hugo/PolittFleuryBiere-SAT2023.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Proof Checking with LRAT in CADICAL (Work in Progress)\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/PollittFleuryBiere-MBMV23.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about cake_lpr, verified LRAT checking, and the SAT competition 2025:\n\n## cake_lpr: Verified LRAT and LPR Proof Checking\n\ncake_lpr is formally verified using CakeML and the HOL4 theorem prover, making it a unique tool in the landscape of SAT proof checkers. The proof checker is formally verified down to the level of its x64 machine code implementation, which eliminates the possibility of bugs arising from compiler errors, code extraction, or other unverified additions.\n\nThe tool introduces a new Linear PR (LPR) proof format that enriches PR proofs with hints and is backwards compatible with the LRAT format, along with a tool to efficiently enrich PR proofs with hints, and cake_lpr—an efficient verified LPR proof checker with correctness guarantees.\n\n## CaDiCaL and SAT Competition 2025\n\nAll proofs generated by CaDiCaL were checked by at least one checker in testing scenarios. Additionally, cake_lpr was presented as a verified LRAT and LPR proof checking tool by Yong Kiam Tan, Marijn J. H. Heule, and Magnus O. Myreen at the SAT Competition 2025.\n\nThe tool has become increasingly important for competition validation, as cake_lpr was used to validate the unsatisfiability proofs in the 2020 SAT Competition because of its strong trust story combined with easy compilation and usage.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"77a822b1-3ba8-4d33-a78b-bb224a01648f","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:06.390Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"862c5ede-5e0c-4cd0-81e1-906e0742dcf6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"702e213f-9852-4a40-af70-a417f3ae3f15","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVmNPBwnvi5nRbrTQD36qJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AlphaProof DeepMind Lean theorem proving 2026 status\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning | Nature\",\"url\":\"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y\"},{\"title\":\"AI achieves silver-medal standard solving International Mathematical Olympiad problems — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/ai-solves-imo-problems-at-silver-medal-level/\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof Paper\",\"url\":\"https://www.julian.ac/blog/2025/11/13/alphaproof-paper/\"},{\"title\":\"Major Breakthroughs in Lean 4-Based Auto-Formalized Mathematics\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.virginia.edu/~rmw7my/Courses/AgenticAISpring2026/Major%20Breakthroughs%20in%20Lean%204-Based%20Auto-Formalized%20Mathematics.html\"},{\"title\":\"Olympiad-level formal mathematical reasoning with reinforcement learning - PubMed\",\"url\":\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/41225005/\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced version of Gemini with Deep Think officially achieves gold-medal standard at the International Mathematical Olympiad — Google DeepMind\",\"url\":\"https://deepmind.google/blog/advanced-version-of-gemini-with-deep-think-officially-achieves-gold-medal-standard-at-the-international-mathematical-olympiad/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google-deepmind/formal-conjectures: A collection of formalized statements of conjectures in Lean. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures\"},{\"title\":\"AlphaProof When RL meets Formal Maths Thomas HUBERT, March 2025\",\"url\":\"https://rdi.berkeley.edu/adv-llm-agents/slides/alphaproof.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"AI math genius delivers 100% accurate results\",\"url\":\"https://phys.org/news/2025-11-ai-math-genius-accurate-results.html\"},{\"title\":\"Lean Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://lean-lang.org/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's the current status of AlphaProof and DeepMind's Lean theorem-proving work as of 2026:\n\n## AlphaProof's Performance\n\nAlphaProof is an RL agent capable of proving complex mathematical problems within the formal environment of the Lean theorem prover, combining an AlphaZero-inspired learning framework with a curriculum of millions of auto-formalized problems and a TTRL approach based on variant generation.\n\n### 2024 IMO Achievement\n\nAlphaProof solved three problems (P1, P2 and P6) at the 2024 IMO, placing the combined system's performance within the silver-medal threshold. AlphaProof managed to discover a proof for P6, the hardest of all the problems for the human participants.\n\n### 2025-2026 Updates\n\nThe field has evolved significantly. Last year (2024), Google DeepMind's combined AlphaProof and AlphaGeometry 2 systems achieved the silver-medal standard, solving four out of the six problems and scoring 28 points. However, an advanced version of Gemini Deep Think solved five out of the six IMO problems perfectly, earning 35 total points, and achieving gold-medal level performance at IMO 2025.\n\nUnlike large language models, AlphaProof guarantees 100% correct solutions by verifying every logical step using the Lean proof assistant.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"61bae154-810e-4384-a0bc-d4774b89d0ff","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:07.485Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"702e213f-9852-4a40-af70-a417f3ae3f15","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
