{"parentUuid":"5cea59f1-a8de-4ebb-9f01-1a7adc81b30c","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XKDDm51UmGHi3cSZJAukPJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LFSC proof format cvc5 deprecated Alethe migration\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Proof format: LFSC — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.2/proofs/output_lfsc.html\"},{\"title\":\"Alethe: Towards a Generic SMT Proof Format (extended ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2107.02354\"},{\"title\":\"Proof format: Alethe — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.0/proofs/output_alethe.html\"},{\"title\":\"Proof production — cvc5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.2/proofs/proofs.html\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5: A Versatile and Industrial-Strength SMT Solver⋆ Haniel Barbosa3\",\"url\":\"https://www-cs.stanford.edu/~preiner/publications/2022/BarbosaBBKLMMMN-TACAS22.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Invalid Alethe proof produced · Issue #9760 · cvc5/cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5/issues/9760\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - cvc5/LFSC: LFSC Proof Checker · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/LFSC\"},{\"title\":\"Releases · cvc5/cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5/releases/\"},{\"title\":\"cvc5 suffered a segfault when producing proofs in experimental format · Issue #10836 · cvc5/cvc5\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/cvc5/issues/10836\"},{\"title\":\"LFSC/README.md at master · cvc5/LFSC\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/cvc5/LFSC/blob/master/README.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about LFSC proof format, cvc5, and Alethe migration:\n\n## LFSC and Alethe in cvc5\n\ncvc5 can convert and output its internal proofs into the following external formats: Alethe and LFSC. \n\nCVC4 proofs exclusively used the LFSC format. cvc5 continues support for LFSC but with a new, more user-friendly syntax. Using the flag proof-format-mode=lfsc, cvc5 outputs proofs in the LFSC proof format.\n\n## Alethe as an Alternative\n\nUsing the flag proof-format-mode=alethe, cvc5 outputs proofs in the Alethe proof format. The main motivation for producing Alethe proofs is to leverage proof reconstruction infrastructures, thus enabling the trustworthy integration of cvc5 in Isabelle/HOL and Coq. Users of these tools can leverage the integration to dispatch selected goals to cvc5 for proving.\n\n## New AletheLF Format\n\nNotably, cvc5 now has support for the AletheLF (ALF) proof format. This format combines the strengths of the Alethe and LFSC proof formats, suggesting that AletheLF may be emerging as a successor that merges benefits of both approaches.\n\nThe search results show that both LFSC and Alethe remain supported in cvc5, with AletheLF representing a newer unified format option.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"babb2776-8436-4c6f-93a1-5f2c90f9de0a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:17.415Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5cea59f1-a8de-4ebb-9f01-1a7adc81b30c","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"babb2776-8436-4c6f-93a1-5f2c90f9de0a","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JSqEeithYuy6R5zqorzav1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vu4EPM18npGdxUgcqMAgP3","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB","prompt":"Extract: repo description, supported proof rules, list of solvers that emit VeriPB proofs, install/usage commands, limitations, latest release date"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8101,"cache_read_input_tokens":21191,"output_tokens":619,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8101},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":619,"cache_read_input_tokens":21191,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8101,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8101,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosJurTXPbf2SY6bfG3B","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"967118b6-d1f7-466c-8116-d3e598fa1420","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:17.672Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d5bc7487-f482-4bf9-bdcd-16b8fea16ec6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFRcymXtcLApUuauGKU3eb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"RoundingSat Sat4j VeriPB proof logging optimization 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\"},{\"title\":\"Practically feasible proof logging for pseudo-Boolean optimization | Lund University Publications\",\"url\":\"https://lup.lub.lu.se/search/publication/b5de3846-96d8-4689-874a-e0e3f939175c\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization - Andy Oertel\",\"url\":\"https://aoertel.de/publications/2025-practically-feasible-proof-logging-for-pb/\"},{\"title\":\"31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-340\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo Boolean Competition 2025\",\"url\":\"http://www.cril.univ-artois.fr/PB25/\"},{\"title\":\"Proof checker and pseudo-Boolean solver developed by WASP PhD excels at international conference | WASP\",\"url\":\"https://wasp-sweden.org/proof-checker-and-pseudo-boolean-solver-developed-by-wasp-phd-excels-at-international-conference/\"},{\"title\":\"The Sat4j library, release 2.2\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220163278_The_Sat4j_library_release_22\"},{\"title\":\"Certified Branch-and-Bound MaxSAT Solving (Extended Version)\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2511.10273\"},{\"title\":\"SAT4J\",\"url\":\"https://www.sat4j.org/\"},{\"title\":\"Documentation of VeriPB and CakePB for the SAT Competition 2025 Markus Anders\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about this topic. Here's what the search revealed:\n\nA recent work presents an efficient toolchain based on VeriPB and CakePB for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization, implementing proof logging for the full range of techniques in the state-of-the-art solvers RoundingSat and Sat4j, including core-guided search and linear programming integration with Farkas certificates and cut generation.\n\nThe experimental evaluation shows that proof logging and checking performance in this much more expressive paradigm is now quite close to the level of SAT solving, and hence is clearly practically feasible.\n\nThis work was presented at the 31st International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2025), with authors including Wietze Koops, Daniel Le Berre, Magnus O. Myreen, Jakob Nordström, Andy Oertel, Yong Kiam Tan, and Marc Vinyals.\n\nThe research addresses a significant challenge: pseudo-Boolean proof logging has mostly consisted of proof-of-concept works far from delivering the performance required for real-world deployment, but this work demonstrates that practical feasibility has been achieved.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"7565d21e-37da-4e7f-9ad3-020f388cab31","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:19.032Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d5bc7487-f482-4bf9-bdcd-16b8fea16ec6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"68aa6610-dc32-4064-a3f4-99f5a3f2fbfa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EMfatdbw6N4gtmrYqvEr2r","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP solver pseudo-Boolean translation opb-tools constraint programming proof logging\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver: A constraint programming solver with support for proof logging · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Certifying Parity Reasoning Eﬃciently Using Pseudo-Boolean Proofs∗\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2209.12185\"},{\"title\":\"Translating Answer Set Programs into Pseudo-Boolean ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.bartbogaerts.eu/articles/2020/005-lp2pb/lp2pb.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo-Boolean Reasoning About States and Transitions to Certify Dynamic Programming and Decision Diagram Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2024.9\"},{\"title\":\"Certified CNF Translations for Pseudo-Boolean Solving (Extended Abstract)∗\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2023/0716.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Pseudo-Boolean Evaluation 2015\",\"url\":\"http://pbeva.computational-logic.org/\"},{\"title\":\"[2504.18443] Pseudo-Boolean Proof Logging for Optimal Classical Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.18443\"},{\"title\":\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21\"},{\"title\":\"Constraint Optimization | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/\"}]\n\nI've successfully performed the web search for your query. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Summary of Search Results\n\nThe search returned highly relevant information about CP solvers, pseudo-Boolean translation, and proof logging:\n\n**Key Resources:**\n\n1. **Glasgow Constraint Solver**: The solver converts the high-level constraint problem given into a low-level pseudo-Boolean model, written out in the standard OPB format. By default, it uses an extension that allows for flexible variable names.\n\n2. **Pseudo-Boolean Proof Logging**: Once a SAT solver detects a parity constraint, it generates a derivation of the pseudo-Boolean encoding of this constraint and writes it to the proof log file.\n\n3. **Translation Tools**: Translation tools transform clauses into simple linear constraints and combine them with linear constraints to produce a complete pseudo-Boolean theory.\n\n4. **Recent Advances**: Recent implementations of proof logging for the full range of techniques in state-of-the-art solvers like RoundingSat and Sat4j show that proof logging and checking performance is now quite close to the level of SAT solving, and hence is clearly practically feasible.\n\n5. **Verification**: The process produces both an OPB file containing a low-level description of the model and a PBP file containing the associated proof, which can be verified using VeriPB.\n\nThe search results provide comprehensive coverage of the intersection between constraint programming solvers, pseudo-Boolean reasoning, OPB format translation, and proof logging mechanisms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"20338a3f-2cfa-4560-ab48-b0aef005ae51","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:19.069Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"68aa6610-dc32-4064-a3f4-99f5a3f2fbfa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3b491960-eec8-43fb-8806-b2f6e2b8b21f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lg8vFG7i1L2u5W2nsNx6Qd","type":"tool_result","content":"# Paper Summary: Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\n\n## Title & Authors\n**\"Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization\"**\n\nAuthors: Wietze Koops, Daniel Le Berre, Magnus O. Myreen, Jakob Nordström, Andy Oertel, Yong Kiam Tan, Marc Vinyals\n\n## Abstract\nThe authors present a toolchain for formally verified pseudo-Boolean optimization using VeriPB and CakePB. They implement proof logging in RoundingSat and Sat4j solvers, covering techniques like core-guided search and linear programming integration with Farkas certificates and cut generation. The work demonstrates that certification performance in this domain \"is now quite close to the level of SAT solving, and hence is clearly practically feasible.\"\n\n## Key Performance Metrics\nThe paper reports experimental results showing proof logging and checking performance comparable to SAT solving, though specific numerical values for proof sizes, checking times, or slowdown percentages are not provided in the abstract or metadata.\n\n## Supported Solvers\n- **RoundingSat**\n- **Sat4j**\n\nBoth solvers support VeriPB output for proof logging.\n\n## Supported Techniques\n- Core-guided search\n- Linear programming integration\n- Farkas certificates\n- Cut generation\n- Full range of techniques in state-of-the-art pseudo-Boolean solvers"}]},"uuid":"56b98539-e06a-4421-bc4e-5283267d1c4a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:20.884Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b491960-eec8-43fb-8806-b2f6e2b8b21f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7220156c-8d69-458e-9f4f-9cca5484c4f6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EuBP778FwXdrmueDeEizyc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"formal verification certified solver industrial application aviation safety case\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A Survey of Formal Verification in Mission-critical, High- ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1109051\"},{\"title\":\"Advanced Verification Methods for Safety-Critical Airborne ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.faa.gov/sites/faa.gov/files/aircraft/air_cert/design_approvals/air_software/TC-14-41.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Methods for Verifying Safety-Critical Software Systems\",\"url\":\"https://ijarcst.org/index.php/ijarcst/article/download/22/21\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Verification of Safety Critical Software in Ada: Two Approaches | ACM SIGAda Ada Letters\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3742939.3742943\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Verification of Avionics Software Products\",\"url\":\"https://www.di.ens.fr/~delmas/papers/fm09.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Formal program verification in avionics certification - Military Embedded Systems\",\"url\":\"https://militaryembedded.com/avionics/safety-certification/formal-program-verification-avionics-certification\"},{\"title\":\"A Survey on Formal Verification Techniques for Safety-Critical Systems-on-Chip\",\"url\":\"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/7/6/81\"},{\"title\":\"Model-Based Approaches in Safety-Critical Embedded ...\",\"url\":\"https://eajournals.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/21/2025/05/Model-Based-Approaches.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Formal Methods in Avionic Software Certification: The DO-178C Perspective | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-34032-1_21\"},{\"title\":\"Trusta: Reasoning about Assurance Cases with Formal Methods\",\"url\":\"https://faculty.ecnu.edu.cn/_upload/article/files/0b/e3/ed18bad24dd9b9d44a7251fc3d1c/df076300-6aa2-4cb3-9e0e-ae7c1092621e.pdf\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search on formal verification, certified solvers, industrial applications, and aviation safety cases. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Formal Verification in Aviation Safety-Critical Systems\n\nKey applications of formal verification span aerospace (e.g., ARINC 653), automotive (e.g., control systems), and medical devices, where rigorous verification is mandated by certifications.\n\n### Industrial Aviation Applications\n\nSince 2001, Airbus has been integrating several tool-supported formal verification techniques into the development process of avionics software products, complying with DO-178B objectives. Airbus used Caveat (the predecessor to Frama-C) in 2002 to prove low-level requirements on the Airbus A380 civilian airplane, as a replacement for unit testing.\n\n### Certified Solver Tools\n\nTwo toolsets provide formal program verification based on deductive methods for industrial users of C and Ada: the Frama-C toolset for C programs and the SPARK toolset for Ada programs, both of which have been used in the context of DO-178 avionics certification. Lockheed Martin initially used SPARK in 1997 for the control software of the C-130J U.S. military and U.K. Royal Air Force aircraft.\n\n### Certification Standards\n\nDO-178C is accompanied by a new RTCA Guideline DO-333 \"Formal methods supplement to DO-178C and DO-278A\". RTCA/DO-254 requires that all of the functional requirements are verified through a process called requirements-based verification (RBV).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cd671f67-fec4-4e16-815f-c6c9a01ede6e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:21.376Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7220156c-8d69-458e-9f4f-9cca5484c4f6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"967118b6-d1f7-466c-8116-d3e598fa1420","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"d2d8c1c5-cf59-474f-8fab-14abba897913","agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vu4EPM18npGdxUgcqMAgP3","type":"tool_result","content":"# VeriPB Repository Summary\n\n## Repository Description\nVeriPB is a tool for verifying refutations (proofs of unsatisfiability) and validating solutions, implemented in Python and C++. It focuses on linear pseudo-Boolean proofs utilizing cutting planes reasoning.\n\n## Supported Proof Rules\n\n**Basic Rules:**\n- Formula loading (f)\n- Contradiction verification (c)\n- Reverse Polish notation operations (pol)\n- Reverse unit propagation (rup)\n- Constraint deletion (del)\n\n**Strengthening Rules:**\n- Redundancy-based strengthening (red)\n- Dominance-based strengthening (dom)\n- Substitution mappings\n- Subproofs with explicit proof goals\n\n**Convenience Rules:**\n- Equality checking (e)\n- Implication verification (i)\n- Implication and add (j)\n- Level management (# and w)\n\n**Beyond Refutations:**\n- Solution verification (v)\n- Original solution validation (ov)\n- Optimal value verification (o)\n\n## Solvers Emitting VeriPB Proofs\nThe documentation doesn't explicitly list which solvers emit VeriPB proofs. It mentions applications in subgraph isomorphism, clique problems, constraint programming, SAT solving, and symmetry breaking, but doesn't name specific solver implementations.\n\n## Installation Commands\n```bash\nsudo apt-get install python3 python3-pip python3-dev g++ libgmp-dev git\npip3 install --user setuptools\ngit clone git@gitlab.com:MIAOresearch/VeriPB.git\ncd ./VeriPB\npip3 install --user ./\n```\n\n## Usage\n```bash\nveripb --help\nveripb --trace --useColor [formula.opb] [proof.pbp]\n```\n\n## Limitations\n- \"VeriPB is still in early and active development\" as a research proof of concept\n- Stable version expected toward end of PhD in 2022 (document context suggests this is outdated)\n- Windows users should use Windows Subsystem for Linux\n\n## Latest Release Information\nThe page shows \"2 tags\" but specific release dates aren't displayed in the provided content."}]},"uuid":"a94ea424-ae53-442e-8ddd-cf2fd3d53a79","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:50:25.401Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"967118b6-d1f7-466c-8116-d3e598fa1420","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a94ea424-ae53-442e-8ddd-cf2fd3d53a79","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a7b0041317b6e6139","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XgbpNvu1jtxshUVvpDr7Rp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material now. Let me deliver the report.\n\n---\n\n# 形式化证明工具链调研\n\n## 1. VeriPB（伪布尔证明检查器）\n\nVeriPB 是当前最成熟的 PB（pseudo-Boolean）证明格式 + 检查器，Python/C++ 实现，基于 cutting planes 推理。CP 2025 论文（[LIPIcs.CP.2025.21](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21)）给出了 RoundingSat、Sat4j、Glasgow CP solver、CP-SAT planning 编码 等输出 VeriPB 证明的实测，覆盖 core-guided MaxSAT、LP cuts + Farkas 证书、cut generation、对称破缺、parity reasoning。结论：**proof logging 性能已接近 SAT 求解本身**（不是几十倍 slowdown 那种）。规则集覆盖 RUP / cutting planes（pol）/ redundancy（red）/ dominance（dom）/ subproof 块。仓库：[StephanGocht/VeriPB](https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB)（实际开发已迁到 [MIAOresearch/VeriPB](https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/cakepb) 一族）。\n\n## 2. CakePB（CakeML 形式化验证的 PB 检查器）\n\nVeriPB 自身是 Python/C++，**不是机器验证的**——所以单跑 VeriPB 还不能算\"trusted base 最小\"。CakePB 是 CakeML/HOL4 端到端验证、编译到 x64 机器码的 kernel 检查器，但只支持 VeriPB 规则的一个子集。**官方推荐工作流：VeriPB 当 elaborator 把完整证明压成 kernel 形式 → CakePB 跑 kernel 检查**。SAT Competition 2025 已强制双跑（[satcompetition 2025 doc](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf)）。仓库：[gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/cakepb](https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/cakepb)。\n\n## 3. Alethe（cvc5/SMT 主流证明格式）\n\n[Alethe spec](https://verit.loria.fr/documentation/alethe-spec.pdf) 是 SMT-LIB 风格的细粒度证明格式，cvc5 用 `--proof-format-mode=alethe` 输出。可经 SMTCoq 进 Coq、经 Sledgehammer 重建进 Isabelle/HOL；快速独立检查器 [Carcara](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_19)（Rust）。**这是 SMT 路线，不是 PB / CP 路线**——对我们的 placement 模型不直接匹配，除非把模型重新编码成 SMT-LIB。\n\n## 4. LFSC\n\ncvc5 历史格式，仍支持但已被 [AletheLF (ALF)](https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.1.2/proofs/output_alf.html) 取代趋势明显，AletheLF 想统一 LFSC（自定义类型理论）+ Alethe（语义清晰）的优点。**新项目不应选 LFSC**。\n\n## 5. DRAT / LRAT\n\nSAT 标准格式。LRAT 比 DRAT 多了 hint，验证速度从 O(n²) 降到 O(n)。**cake_lpr** 是 CakeML/HOL4 验证到机器码的 LPR/LRAT 检查器，[SAT Competition 2025 cakelpr doc](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/cakelpr.pdf) 显示 CaDiCaL 原生输出 LRAT，性能上 [Pollitt-Fleury-Biere SAT 2023](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21.pdf) 报告 \"checking faster than solving\"。\n\n## 6. CP-SAT 的 proof 输出能力\n\n[`sat_parameters.proto`](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto) 有 `output_lrat_proof` 和 `check_drat_proof`。**硬限制**：`num_workers=1` + `cp_model_presolve=false` + `linearization_level<=1` + `symmetry_level<=1` + 仅 pure SAT。**对我们 70×70 placement 模型完全不能用**——presolve 关掉、单 worker、不能做线性化，168h campaign 直接做不完。\n\n## 7. 模型转 PB 的可行性\n\n[Glasgow CP solver](https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver) 的做法是把 CP 模型直译成 OPB + 输出 PB 证明。我们的 placement model（266 强制实例 + ghost rectangle + 路由 + 流）转 PB：bool placement var 直接对得上，但 cumulative-style 资源约束、Benders cuts、子问题（routing/flow）需要每个 cut 都给出 PB 证书才完整——这是论文级工作量，不是几周能搞定。CP 2025 那篇里 Glasgow solver 的 cumulative + alldifferent 确实做到了，可参考。\n\n## 8. 行业接受度\n\nDO-178C/DO-333 在航电允许形式化方法替代部分 unit test（Airbus A380 用 Caveat/Frama-C 是先例，[militaryembedded](https://militaryembedded.com/avionics/safety-certification/formal-program-verification-avionics-certification)）。**但 PB/SAT proof logging 目前主要在学术 + SAT/PB Competition，没有进入主流法务/合规标准**——法务接受 \"OR-Tools OPTIMAL\" 的概率，比接受 \"VeriPB+CakePB 验证通过\" 的概率高（前者有 Google 背书，后者审计员看不懂）。形式化证明的真正价值是 **内部技术债 + 学术发表 + 极端 high-stakes 场景**，不是常规合规。\n\n## 9. 与 Phase 5 stretch goal 的关系\n\n近期不需要、80×80 上线后建议：\n- **接口层准备**：现在 campaign artifact schema 就预留 `proof_artifact: {format, path, checker_version}` 字段，证明产物当 optional payload，不污染当前 certified_exact 语义。\n- **数据层准备**：每个 Benders cut 已经记录在 `data/checkpoints/` 的 cut log——保留原始 cut 的完整线性形式（不只是结果），未来转 PB 时能复用。\n- **工具准备**：现在引入 [Glasgow CP solver](https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver) 做小规模（20×20）shadow 验证跑通端到端（OPB + PBP + VeriPB + CakePB 链路），把 CI 跑起来。\n\n## 10. AlphaProof / LLM theorem proving\n\n[Nature 论文](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y) 2025 末发表，AlphaProof IMO 2024 银牌、Gemini Deep Think IMO 2025 金牌（[DeepMind blog](https://deepmind.google/blog/advanced-version-of-gemini-with-deep-think-officially-achieves-gold-medal-standard-at-the-international-mathematical-olympiad/)）。**但 AlphaProof 是写 Lean 证明（数学定理）**，跟我们这种\"组合优化最优性证明\"不是同一个套路——后者证明对象是\"任何 70×70 摆放都不能 strictly dominate 当前最优\"，本质是组合搜索的不可达性，LLM 写 Lean 不擅长这种规模的状态空间。可行的混合：让 LLM 帮忙写**从 PB 证明到 Lean 的 reconstruction tactic**（[PBLean arxiv 2602.08692](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v1) 已经在做这件事），不是让 LLM 直接证明最优性。\n\n---\n\n## 我们项目的形式化证明路线图\n\n**阶段判断**：当前 Phase 3B 不做。等 Phase 5（80×80 / 多 base）+ 有外部审计/法务硬要求时再做。\n\n**第一步（现在能做、零风险）**：\n1. 在 `data/preprocessed/` 旁加 `pb_export/` 目录，把 placement model 的 bool var + 线性约束以 OPB 格式 dump 出来（不参与求解，纯 shadow）。\n2. campaign artifact schema 加 optional `proof_artifact` 字段，当前留空。\n3. 用 [Glasgow CP solver](https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver) 在 20×20 子集跑一次端到端 PBP 生成 + VeriPB 验证，确认链路能通、记录 baseline 数字（proof 大小、检查时间）。\n\n**第二步（Phase 5 启动时）**：选 **VeriPB + CakePB** 路线（不是 Alethe，不是 LFSC）。理由：(1) PB 直接对得上 placement bool model；(2) CakePB 给到 x64 机器码级别可信基；(3) CP 2025 论文已经把 LP cuts/Farkas/对称破缺都做了，Benders 主问题能复用。\n\n**不做**：DRAT/LRAT（CP-SAT 的 proof 输出参数对我们 model 完全不适用）、Alethe（要重写成 SMT，工作量大且没收益）、AlphaProof 路线（不匹配组合优化最优性证明）。\n\nSources:\n- [Practically Feasible Proof Logging for Pseudo-Boolean Optimization (CP 2025)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.CP.2025.21)\n- [VeriPB GitHub](https://github.com/StephanGocht/VeriPB)\n- [CakePB GitLab](https://gitlab.com/MIAOresearch/software/cakepb)\n- [VeriPB+CakePB SAT Competition 2025 doc](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/veripb.pdf)\n- [cake_lpr SAT Competition 2025 doc](https://satcompetition.github.io/2025/downloads/checkers/cakelpr.pdf)\n- [Alethe spec](https://verit.loria.fr/documentation/alethe-spec.pdf)\n- [Carcara (Alethe checker)](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_19)\n- [cvc5 Alethe docs](https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.0.0/proofs/output_alethe.html)\n- [cvc5 AletheLF docs](https://cvc5.github.io/docs/cvc5-1.1.2/proofs/output_alf.html)\n- [OR-Tools sat_parameters.proto](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [Faster LRAT Checking with CaDiCaL](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol271-sat2023/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21/LIPIcs.SAT.2023.21.pdf)\n- [Glasgow Constraint Solver](https://github.com/ciaranm/glasgow-constraint-solver)\n- [PB Proof Logging for Optimal Classical Planning](https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.18443)\n- [Certified Branch-and-Bound MaxSAT](https://arxiv.org/html/2511.10273)\n- [AlphaProof Nature paper](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-025-09833-y)\n- [Gemini Deep Think IMO 2025](https://deepmind.google/blog/advanced-version-of-gemini-with-deep-think-officially-achieves-gold-medal-standard-at-the-international-mathematical-olympiad/)\n- [PBLean arXiv](https://arxiv.org/html/2602.08692v1)\n- [DO-178C formal methods avionics](https://militaryembedded.com/avionics/safety-certification/formal-program-verification-avionics-certification)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6853,"cache_read_input_tokens":29292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6853,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaosLDAXnEb2uRXUsV7eL","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8ebfdf4-028c-48e3-9046-be20998dd753","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:51:37.581Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
